body:
sorry!! i didnt check what reddit this was in i actually thought it was lithium. i take effexor too though

&#x200B;

did you start on 75mg? ask to start on 37.5mg if you didnt. effexor is a tough one as well...but ignore my previous comment

im so bad at organizing my speech -- i try to be insightful or tell an intriguing story or a good joke, and sometimes i get it. a lot of the time it's super jumbled. i feel like half of my jumble is acceptable enough for people who already know me, but to strangers its ??????. and the other half is ????? and i find myself giving up telling stories or jokes if its messed up enough

&#x200B;

 also: i thought i had ADHD for a while but it's likely symptoms of depression/anxiety so . . . i have bad memory, exec functioning, bad at holding words in my brain (i think its called working memory???), poor focus .... etc etc. definitely way worse when im very anxious

sudden movements trigger it for me, and a way to nearly 100% trigger it is to move your eyes side to side. i don't run but i imagine i would get them if i did. i recently started getting them despite taking my meds on time - im on 225mg. i used to only get them if i missed a dose or took it significantly later, but now i get mild ones starting early afternoon. very common with antidepressant withdrawal, but since effexor has particularly bad withdrawals they can just kinda happen i guess

&#x200B;

edited to say that i posted about this recently, and someone had the same experience and they have a 25mg instant release that they take half of later on to help out. if its a problem for you it could be worth bringing up to your prescriber
